# Generated files are not authored, so neither side of a merge is
# authoritative: the merged TREE is, and a generator is the function from
# the tree to the file. A merge therefore never stops on one: the driver merges the text when it can and keeps OURS when it
# cannot, and `delendai guard post-merge` regenerates from the finished
# tree and commits what moved. A file with a generated region inside it
# (the two READMEs) has its authored text merged for real.
#
# The driver is configured per clone by `delendai guard install`. Without
# it git simply merges these files as before, so a clone that has not run
# the installer is no worse off than today.
#
# Every `gen:all` step must be routed here; the spec of the driver fails
# when one is not.
